CM ============================================================
CM PERFORMANCE COMPARISON GUIDE:
CM
CM Run trapped and reference models at same frequency and height.
CM Compare: maximum gain (dBi), feedpoint impedance, pattern shape.
CM
CM Expected trap losses (vs untrapped reference):
CM  Band   Trap Q    Expected Loss
CM  10M    ~55       1.5-2.5 dBd
CM  15M    ~63       1.0-2.0 dBd
CM  20M    ~77       0.5-1.5 dBd
CM  40M    ~109      0.3-0.8 dBd
CM  80M    ~151      0.5-1.0 dBd (40M traps only in path)
CM
CM Trap loss formula (per trap in antenna path):
CM  Loss_dB ≈ 8.686 * (R_series / R_radiation)
CM  where R_series = omega*L/Q for the series equivalent
CM
CM NOTE: Pattern shape should be nearly identical to reference dipole.
CM Traps do NOT significantly alter radiation pattern at design frequencies.
CM ============================================================
